# Refactor: Duplicated dev/prod blocks → one module with `for_each`

## Before (duplicated)

```hcl
# main.tf — dev
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "dev_assets" { bucket = "app-assets-dev" ... }
resource "aws_db_instance" "dev_db" { instance_class = "db.t3.micro" ... }

# main.tf — prod (near-identical copy)
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "prod_assets" { bucket = "app-assets-prod" ... }
resource "aws_db_instance" "prod_db" { instance_class = "db.t3.medium" ... }
```

## After

### `environments.tf` — single source of truth

```hcl
locals {
  envs = {
    dev = {
      region         = "us-east-1"
      node_count     = 2
      instance_types = ["t3.medium"]
      db_class       = "db.t3.micro"
      db_multi_az    = false
      db_encrypted   = false
      bucket_versioning = true
      replication    = null
    }
    prod = {
      region         = "us-east-2"
      node_count     = 4
      instance_types = ["t3.large"]
      db_class       = "db.t3.medium"
      db_multi_az    = true
      db_encrypted   = true
      bucket_versioning = true
      replication    = { destination = "us-west-2" }
    }
  }
}

module "env" {
  source   = "./modules/env"
  for_each = local.envs

  env             = each.key
  region          = each.value.region
  node_count      = each.value.node_count
  instance_types  = each.value.instance_types
  db_class        = each.value.db_class
  db_multi_az     = each.value.db_multi_az
  db_encrypted    = each.value.db_encrypted
  replication     = each.value.replication
  db_password     = try(data.sops_file.secrets[each.key].raw["db_password"], null)
}
```

### `modules/env/main.tf` (condensed)

```hcl
variable "env" {}
variable "region" {}
# ... sizing vars, validation on db_class etc.

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "assets" {
  bucket = "app-assets-${var.env}"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_versioning" "assets" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  versioning_configuration { status = "Enabled" }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration" "assets" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  rule { apply_server_side_encryption_by_default { sse_algorithm = "AES256" } }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block" "assets" {
  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  block_public_acls       = true
  block_public_policy     = true
  ignore_public_acls      = true
  restrict_public_buckets = true
}

# replication block only when var.replication != null
resource "aws_db_instance" "db" {
  identifier           = "app-db-${var.env}"
  instance_class       = var.db_class
  multi_az             = var.db_multi_az
  storage_encrypted    = var.db_encrypted
  deletion_protection  = true
  backup_retention_period = 7
  publicly_accessible = false
}

# EKS module with managed node groups sized from vars, IAM role with OIDC trust, etc.
```

## Zero-diff state moves

Add `moved` blocks (or generate them with `tfmigrate`):

```hcl
moved {
  from = aws_s3_bucket.dev_assets
  to   = module.env["dev"].aws_s3_bucket.assets
}
moved {
  from = aws_db_instance.dev_db
  to   = module.env["dev"].aws_db_instance.db
}
moved {
  from = aws_s3_bucket.prod_assets
  to   = module.env["prod"].aws_s3_bucket.assets
}
moved {
  from = aws_db_instance.prod_db
  to   = module.env["prod"].aws_db_instance.db
}
# ...one moved block per original resource
```

## Verification (must be zero-diff)

```bash
terraform init
terraform plan -var-file=envs/dev.tfvars   # "No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration."
terraform plan -var-file=envs/prod.tfvars  # same
```

## Key points

- **Environment isolation**: `for_each` creates separate addresses per env; `module.env["prod"]` changes never touch dev state.
- **Secrets**: DB password via SOPS-encrypted file (`data "sops_file"`), never plaintext in tfvars.
- **Least privilege**: no wildcard actions; IAM trust uses EKS OIDC provider for prod.
- **Optional features** (replication, encryption, multi-AZ) keyed off env vars, not duplicated blocks.
- Keep the `moved` blocks indefinitely in git history — don't delete them after the first apply, or downstream branches will drift.
